1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:02:03,461
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:05,624 --> 00:02:08,687
NO LIVING CREATURE WAS HARMED
DURING THE FILMING OF THIS SHOW.

3
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:36,347
Those tyrants are using our warriors
against us.

4
00:02:36,923 --> 00:02:41,600
Come back to your true self, Göktuğ.

5
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:45,893
Don't forget, everything turns to it's
essence.

6
00:02:46,577 --> 00:02:50,187
A dog is a dog, a wolf is a wolf!

7
00:02:56,992 --> 00:02:59,372
Look, I have the same thing on me.

8
00:02:59,542 --> 00:03:03,307
Of course, you have, son. All of our
warriors have that.

9
00:03:05,773 --> 00:03:10,955
Balgay... You will pay for it, Balgay.

10
00:03:37,088 --> 00:03:41,215
Your tears can't put out the fire
of your heart, brother.

11
00:03:46,173 --> 00:03:51,628
I remember everything, one by one.
Our father...

12
00:03:54,367 --> 00:03:56,700
Our mother...

13
00:04:00,088 --> 00:04:02,284
What Mongols had done...

14
00:04:08,846 --> 00:04:12,933
As long as this craven Balgay
lives, every breath is a sin for me.

15
00:04:15,793 --> 00:04:18,212
What are you doing, Göktuğ?
Wait, brother.

16
00:04:18,393 --> 00:04:22,423
I'll go there. I'll skin him alive.

17
00:04:22,998 --> 00:04:26,365
I'll watch him bleed out until the last
drop of his blood, brother.

18
00:04:29,601 --> 00:04:31,757
It's not the time to kill Balgay,
brother.

19
00:04:33,053 --> 00:04:34,621
What are you saying, brother?

20
00:04:34,625 --> 00:04:36,940
What are you saying after all he
has done?

21
00:04:37,624 --> 00:04:38,568
Brother...

22
00:04:40,549 --> 00:04:44,340
Sometimes, having your enemy alive is
better than being dead.

23
00:04:47,765 --> 00:04:49,154
We need him alive for now.

24
00:04:52,794 --> 00:04:56,009
You know, we made an alliance with him.

25
00:04:58,792 --> 00:05:03,167
You will act as nothing happened.
You will, so that...

26
00:05:03,808 --> 00:05:05,657
...we will strike him at a
good moment.

27
00:05:08,185 --> 00:05:12,879
All those years that went to waste,
that you spent far from your essence...

28
00:05:14,225 --> 00:05:17,911
...can only be recovered by the goodness
of penitence.

29
00:05:20,657 --> 00:05:23,391
Now, repeat after me...

30
00:05:27,458 --> 00:05:30,458
Eşhedü en la ilahe illallah...

31
00:05:31,445 --> 00:05:34,226
Eşhedü en la ilahe illallah...

32
00:05:35,090 --> 00:05:38,749
...ve eşhedü enla Muhammeden
abdühü ve rasulü.

33
00:05:39,668 --> 00:05:44,432
...ve eşhedü enla Muhammeden
abdühü ve rasulü.

34
00:06:08,504 --> 00:06:12,212
You should've seen Osman's face
when he found out that Zorba is dead.

35
00:06:13,142 --> 00:06:15,696
His anger grew. It was like
he couldn't control it.

36
00:06:17,742 --> 00:06:20,883
Osman's heart is great.
He is inclusive.

37
00:06:21,661 --> 00:06:24,499
But so is his wrath.

38
00:06:26,167 --> 00:06:29,590
He won't give up on this before
confronting Dündar.

39
00:06:32,489 --> 00:06:37,810
End of this confrontation is clear,
Selcan Hatun. It won't be silent.

40
00:06:39,798 --> 00:06:42,262
Wow... Selcan Hatun.

41
00:06:43,158 --> 00:06:44,479
Yes, Burçin.

42
00:06:45,037 --> 00:06:46,908
The fur flew.

43
00:06:47,265 --> 00:06:49,200
Osman Bey screamed the place down.

44
00:06:50,866 --> 00:06:53,140
You are sitting here.

45
00:06:56,257 --> 00:07:01,959
We don't compete to learn and
involve in everything.

46
00:07:02,457 --> 00:07:05,934
So, we learn what we need
when the time comes.

47
00:07:07,079 --> 00:07:11,396
If so, you shouldn't hear
it from me.

48
00:07:11,624 --> 00:07:15,822
Burçin... Say what you want
to say.

49
00:07:16,317 --> 00:07:18,520
I said you shouldn't hear it from me.

50
00:07:24,979 --> 00:07:31,024
Burçin... I owe so much to your deceased
mother. That's why I bear you.

51
00:07:31,207 --> 00:07:34,897
But don't try your luck. Say what you
will.

52
00:07:36,561 --> 00:07:41,972
Well, since you want it so much...
I should say it.

53
00:07:42,993 --> 00:07:48,403
It wasn't good to see Osman saying that
on the day Aygül was about to marry.

54
00:07:54,649 --> 00:07:57,271
What...did Osman do?

55
00:07:57,711 --> 00:08:02,442
What do you think? Osman Bey came to
the tents with great rage.

56
00:08:03,774 --> 00:08:08,483
He turned the place upside down by saying
''I won't let you marry Aygül to Alişar''

57
00:08:12,837 --> 00:08:16,773
Burçin, what are you speaking,
my daughter?

58
00:08:18,756 --> 00:08:21,732
What business would Osman has with
Aygül's marriage?

59
00:08:24,499 --> 00:08:29,804
I don't know about that. Bamsı Bey and
Gündüz Bey barely managed to stop him.

60
00:08:30,356 --> 00:08:34,742
They told him that he went beyond limit...
They didn't say enough but anyways.

61
00:08:36,083 --> 00:08:40,122
What did Osman tell to Dündar that
made him went beyond the limit?

62
00:08:41,965 --> 00:08:45,745
''I won't let Aygül marry to Alişar''
he said.

63
00:08:50,408 --> 00:08:53,000
-What else did he say?
-What else should he say?

64
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,510
That was all his problem, after all.

65
00:08:56,460 --> 00:08:58,631
What problem did Osman Bey
has with Aygül?

66
00:08:59,135 --> 00:09:01,968
Eh... After all the hurly-burly...

67
00:09:02,278 --> 00:09:05,074
...Dündar Bey spoke at last.

68
00:09:05,498 --> 00:09:09,007
He revealed an old secret.

69
00:09:11,957 --> 00:09:15,690
It seems that back in time he gave Aygül
to Osman.

70
00:09:19,195 --> 00:09:23,876
It's obvious that Osman regretted it so
that he had done all these.

71
00:09:31,901 --> 00:09:34,483
You hit my nerve, Selcan Hatun.

72
00:09:34,872 --> 00:09:37,965
I said I shouldn't speak. You wanted it.

73
00:10:17,931 --> 00:10:22,788
Look after Osman, my nephew.
He threatens us openly.

74
00:10:23,016 --> 00:10:26,308
His anger controls him, uncle.

75
00:10:35,188 --> 00:10:38,630
What's wrong, son?
What's on your mind?

76
00:10:38,757 --> 00:10:40,603
Our anger is so strong, Bamsı Bey.

77
00:10:44,129 --> 00:10:47,692
But if we lose our control to anger...

78
00:10:49,212 --> 00:10:51,169
...it will harm us.

79
00:10:52,310 --> 00:10:55,855
What will we do, brother?
What do you mean?

80
00:10:56,039 --> 00:10:59,931
If we take my uncle in front
of the Tent, blood will be spillt.

81
00:11:01,950 --> 00:11:06,625
We'll carry the banner of mercy like
we carry the banner of courage.

82
00:11:07,387 --> 00:11:12,483
My uncle can't see further from the smoke
in front of him. Let him go to the wedding.

83
00:11:13,095 --> 00:11:17,344
Alright, brother. But, what if we
help Alişar by doing that?

84
00:11:17,989 --> 00:11:22,042
Alişar can think that he has everyone
in his hands...

85
00:11:22,429 --> 00:11:25,113
And we won't be seen together...

86
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:27,360
...so, my uncle can get closer to you.

87
00:11:27,463 --> 00:11:30,533
And then? Then what, son?
What's on your mind?

88
00:11:31,717 --> 00:11:36,758
I'll confront my uncle with Alişar
to show that I didn't kill Batur.

89
00:11:38,006 --> 00:11:40,823
So we will get rid of this boil
for good.

90
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:45,135
-How will this happen, brother?
-Thanks to Aygül, brother.

91
00:11:45,981 --> 00:11:50,556
If everything comes to Aygül...
If Alişar plays all his games on Aygül...

92
00:11:51,359 --> 00:11:55,075
So, we'll break all his games by Aygül.

93
00:11:56,194 --> 00:11:57,903
Osman doesn't know what he speaks.

94
00:11:58,771 --> 00:12:01,504
He does, nephew.
He does.

95
00:12:02,224 --> 00:12:04,756
Look, I'm telling you.

96
00:12:05,387 --> 00:12:08,081
If he tries to stop the feast...

97
00:12:08,493 --> 00:12:13,275
...you should know that we won't
have any more words to speak.

98
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:16,056
When the dust rises up...

99
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:19,667
...eyes can't see clearly, Dündar Bey.

100
00:12:19,952 --> 00:12:21,842
What more should I do, Bamsı Bey?

101
00:12:22,965 --> 00:12:25,414
I tried to be his uncle...

102
00:12:26,296 --> 00:12:29,574
...I tried to be his father...

103
00:12:30,523 --> 00:12:35,814
...now he faces me and tells me that
I can't give Aygül to Alişar.

104
00:12:37,155 --> 00:12:41,362
He went completely crazy.

105
00:12:42,274 --> 00:12:45,059
If something happens to us,
it's on him.

106
00:12:47,658 --> 00:12:51,868
Now, you steel yourself, Dündar Bey.

107
00:12:52,515 --> 00:12:57,543
-I will try talking to him.
-That would be good.

108
00:12:58,202 --> 00:13:01,208
He listens to your words, Bamsı Bey.

109
00:13:01,762 --> 00:13:05,147
I couldn't find time in the rush.

110
00:13:06,497 --> 00:13:11,491
One of you is the Bey of my tents,
and the other is...

111
00:13:12,335 --> 00:13:14,210
...the elder of my tents.

112
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:18,627
I hope you won't leave me alone
in the feast.

113
00:13:22,589 --> 00:13:25,570
Don't worry, uncle.

114
00:13:25,990 --> 00:13:28,035
I won't leave you and Aygül alone.

115
00:13:29,674 --> 00:13:33,412
-We'll be there at the wedding feast.
-Thank you, thank you.

116
00:13:40,474 --> 00:13:44,646
Father, let me come with you.
The road isn't safe.

117
00:13:46,334 --> 00:13:50,335
Do you still say ''father''
without any shame?

118
00:13:55,607 --> 00:13:58,072
Are there any other danger than
your existence?

119
00:13:58,417 --> 00:13:59,504
No need.

120
00:14:00,204 --> 00:14:03,147
Keep your shadow away,
I want nothing more.

121
00:14:18,029 --> 00:14:20,504
He doesn't want me, Gündüz Bey.

122
00:14:21,756 --> 00:14:24,491
Let the wedding feast begin...

123
00:14:25,289 --> 00:14:27,849
...maybe his heart can soften up.

124
00:14:50,373 --> 00:14:51,706
Osman...

125
00:14:59,418 --> 00:15:00,860
Maşallah.

126
00:15:10,969 --> 00:15:13,017
I see you alive like this...

127
00:15:14,017 --> 00:15:15,846
...I'm very happy, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

128
00:15:16,126 --> 00:15:17,791
Thank you, Osman.

129
00:15:28,291 --> 00:15:29,441
Mashallah.

130
00:15:30,097 --> 00:15:33,304
Ghazi's white beard swing like
battle banners, my bey.

131
00:15:34,693 --> 00:15:37,600
He is powerful than any other soldiers.

132
00:15:39,011 --> 00:15:44,223
There still are many weapons to swing
and many tyrants to beat, Osman.

133
00:15:44,662 --> 00:15:47,719
One who follows the true path
always finds companions.

134
00:15:48,462 --> 00:15:51,919
So, Abdurrahman Ghazi, tell me
about this thing.

135
00:15:53,659 --> 00:15:56,484
Who is behind this cowardice?

136
00:15:57,139 --> 00:16:00,897
Allah knows... I thought of Balgay
when we were ambushed.

137
00:16:01,435 --> 00:16:04,568
But it was Alişar.

138
00:16:10,615 --> 00:16:12,475
Alişar...

139
00:16:14,459 --> 00:16:16,428
Don't kill Abdurrahman Ghazi.

140
00:16:16,711 --> 00:16:18,813
And his right-hand man is on it.

141
00:16:20,143 --> 00:16:22,220
Dündar didn't want us to be killed.

142
00:16:22,570 --> 00:16:24,806
But Alişar took him away.

143
00:16:28,060 --> 00:16:29,719
Alişar...

144
00:16:34,461 --> 00:16:37,073
So, Alişar wants to oppress my uncle.

145
00:16:37,916 --> 00:16:41,899
-It's true, Osman
-Things became complicated.

146
00:16:42,768 --> 00:16:44,908
Nothing is complicated, Boran.

147
00:16:46,418 --> 00:16:48,606
Alişar is behind every evil.

148
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:53,351
Allah knows that he is responsible for
Batur's death, as well.

149
00:16:54,065 --> 00:16:57,824
Not only Batur's death but also
abduction of Princess Adelfa...

150
00:16:59,530 --> 00:17:01,988
...and that Zorba incident.

151
00:17:03,748 --> 00:17:06,380
Zorba was his closest man.

152
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:11,531
He must have known something
that Alişar didn't want us to learn.

153
00:17:11,741 --> 00:17:14,285
And seen things that Alişar
didn't want us to see.

154
00:17:17,324 --> 00:17:19,315
So, he sacrificed him.

155
00:17:20,179 --> 00:17:22,979
So, Osman, what is the
role of Dündar?

156
00:17:24,527 --> 00:17:26,780
He'll say that.

157
00:17:27,762 --> 00:17:32,374
But all the mysteries come together
on the name of Alişar.

158
00:17:33,172 --> 00:17:35,812
What will we do, my Bey?
What's on your mind?

159
00:17:36,104 --> 00:17:39,379
We'll teach Alişar not to play with us.

160
00:17:43,618 --> 00:17:45,603
-Abdurrahman Ghazi.
-Yes, Osman.

161
00:17:45,755 --> 00:17:47,845
You go to the mansion with
Kılıç Alp.

162
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:51,234
Follow him until he falls
to my trap.

163
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:54,875
Alright, Osman.

164
00:17:55,566 --> 00:17:56,453
Kılıç.

165
00:18:19,688 --> 00:18:22,442
I had the best room prepared for you,
Commander Böke.

166
00:18:22,975 --> 00:18:25,709
Have a rest. Then we'll talk about
what happened.

167
00:18:25,890 --> 00:18:28,448
You have your grave prepared.

168
00:18:29,173 --> 00:18:32,898
When Geyhatu learns what happened,
he will have you buried alive in there.

169
00:18:34,029 --> 00:18:37,756
Will I answer for your clumsiness,
Commander Böke?

170
00:18:50,874 --> 00:18:53,934
You are at least as much as responsible
of this as I am.

171
00:18:55,289 --> 00:18:59,656
Our secret associate with Sofia is no
longer a secret.

172
00:19:03,498 --> 00:19:07,149
Geyhatu will ask for this from
both of us.

173
00:19:12,546 --> 00:19:15,248
We'll clean this mess together.

174
00:19:16,903 --> 00:19:18,143
How?

175
00:19:18,313 --> 00:19:20,773
We'll find Osman and kill him.

176
00:19:23,003 --> 00:19:25,361
We will do it together.

177
00:19:26,705 --> 00:19:30,040
Do you think that Osman's corpse can
revive ours?

178
00:19:35,764 --> 00:19:40,335
I haven't played my last move yet.

179
00:19:42,415 --> 00:19:45,732
I'll make contact with Sofia and do what
needs to be done.

180
00:19:46,784 --> 00:19:50,056
Osman will die. He must.

181
00:19:51,056 --> 00:19:53,999
Osman is more dangerous than we think.

182
00:19:59,362 --> 00:20:02,949
Osman captured Genghis Khan's Law.

183
00:20:03,561 --> 00:20:06,347
He stopped Geyhatu and Princess Adelfa's
marriage.

184
00:20:07,091 --> 00:20:11,251
He found the tracks of Margareth Monks.

185
00:20:14,794 --> 00:20:18,491
He can't do it all alone.

186
00:20:20,715 --> 00:20:23,766
He wasn't alone. He had someone with him.

187
00:20:23,973 --> 00:20:28,169
-Who was it?
-His uncle. Sungur Tekin

188
00:20:48,973 --> 00:20:51,455
All troubles are after me.

189
00:20:52,469 --> 00:20:55,379
-What is the situation?
-It will be done in a minute, my Bey.

190
00:20:55,996 --> 00:20:59,579
C'mon, hurry. Alişar Bey is waiting
for us.

191
00:21:01,692 --> 00:21:05,549
I told you that Alişar is not a friend!
But what have you done?

192
00:21:06,424 --> 00:21:11,198
You took shelter under him. But it
wasn't enough, you also gave him Aygül.

193
00:21:11,682 --> 00:21:14,757
If you cared so much of Aygül...

194
00:21:14,942 --> 00:21:18,772
...then, when I told you to take her
as your wife...

195
00:21:18,949 --> 00:21:21,929
...why did you refuse?
-I have spoken.

196
00:21:26,450 --> 00:21:29,769
You should know that I won't let
Aygül marry Alişar.

197
00:21:52,209 --> 00:21:53,519
Daughter...

198
00:21:55,209 --> 00:21:57,178
Don't be sad.

199
00:21:57,733 --> 00:22:01,515
It's a good thing. Horses can rest a bit.

200
00:22:02,812 --> 00:22:05,648
The vision of my brother Batur doesn't
go away, father.

201
00:22:06,921 --> 00:22:09,273
He isn't with me in this happiest
day of mine.

202
00:22:12,206 --> 00:22:13,752
If he was here...

203
00:22:14,730 --> 00:22:17,201
...would we be destitute like this?

204
00:22:19,462 --> 00:22:21,992
He would be on your side.

205
00:22:22,976 --> 00:22:25,828
He wouldn't let his sister be in that
state.

206
00:22:29,394 --> 00:22:33,409
I put my valiant son to the grave,
all alone.

207
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:40,481
I'm taking my precious daughter
groom's house, all alone.

208
00:22:43,479 --> 00:22:47,772
I'm like a parasite... In my own home.

209
00:22:54,350 --> 00:22:57,660
For sure, this darkness won't last
forever.

210
00:22:58,697 --> 00:23:02,897
Also, we've seen our real friends
and real enemies.

211
00:23:03,646 --> 00:23:06,681
-We did.
-We did.

212
00:23:06,878 --> 00:23:08,363
We did, thanks to Allah.

213
00:23:08,881 --> 00:23:09,881
We did.

214
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:14,254
Those who stood with me on my
bad times...

215
00:23:14,909 --> 00:23:17,450
...those who didn't stand with me
on my light times...

216
00:23:17,641 --> 00:23:20,001
They are all written down.

217
00:23:21,972 --> 00:23:23,911
Not only Osman...

218
00:23:24,441 --> 00:23:27,800
...whoever stands with him...

219
00:23:28,180 --> 00:23:32,367
...I will confront everyone who
put us into this situation.

220
00:23:33,604 --> 00:23:34,945
I will...

221
00:23:39,925 --> 00:23:41,363
But...

222
00:23:41,963 --> 00:23:44,933
...you shouldn't be sad today,
my pretty daughter.

223
00:23:45,427 --> 00:23:47,500
You should smile.

224
00:23:48,972 --> 00:23:53,053
Smile... Smile, so your father can
always remember you like that.

225
00:23:57,610 --> 00:24:00,467
Smile... So, this helpless Dündar who has
you married...

226
00:24:01,581 --> 00:24:04,909
...can heal his heart a little bit.

227
00:24:11,929 --> 00:24:13,394
Come on.

228
00:25:33,403 --> 00:25:37,403
My brother once said that
Osman Bey's compassion...

229
00:25:38,684 --> 00:25:40,884
... is as strong as his sword.

230
00:25:45,982 --> 00:25:49,472
Forgive me for my inhumaneness, Osman Bey.

231
00:25:54,308 --> 00:25:56,448
Give your blessings.

232
00:26:08,441 --> 00:26:13,831
From now on, in my eyes...

233
00:26:16,954 --> 00:26:18,554
...you're the same with Konur.

234
00:26:20,586 --> 00:26:25,076
Welcome to your roots, Göktuğ.

235
00:26:36,862 --> 00:26:39,082
I have other news, my Bey.

236
00:26:40,360 --> 00:26:45,670
My brother not only returned
to his roots...

237
00:26:46,938 --> 00:26:50,078
... he also chose the true
religion of Islam and became a Muslim.

238
00:26:50,843 --> 00:26:53,213
Praise be!

239
00:26:58,491 --> 00:27:00,951
May Allah keep you in
the right path, brother.

240
00:27:04,373 --> 00:27:08,373
Being your Alp, being enlightened with
the light of Islam...

241
00:27:09,205 --> 00:27:11,355
... is my greatest honour.

242
00:27:13,232 --> 00:27:15,752
May Allah always keep you with us.

243
00:27:16,362 --> 00:27:20,222
May the rest of my life be
ruined on your path, Osman Bey.

244
00:27:20,412 --> 00:27:23,832
Thank you, Göktuğ brother.
Thank you.

245
00:27:25,492 --> 00:27:27,194
Now, brothers...

246
00:27:29,781 --> 00:27:36,241
Listen to me carefully. Dündar Bey is
going to the mansion with the dowry car.

247
00:27:36,941 --> 00:27:40,941
The Alps have loosened the car's wheel.
They will need to stop.

248
00:27:42,696 --> 00:27:46,696
And then we will ambush
my uncle and his family.

249
00:27:46,991 --> 00:27:51,531
My Bey, Dündar Bey will resist.
What will we do?

250
00:27:51,938 --> 00:27:56,678
I want him alive.
I need him alive.

251
00:27:58,178 --> 00:28:03,328
But Alişar will get the news fast.

252
00:28:03,652 --> 00:28:06,982
Abdurrahman Gazi is after that dog.

253
00:28:08,171 --> 00:28:14,491
Konur. Once Alişar leaves the mansion,
you will get Princess Adelfa from there.

254
00:28:15,031 --> 00:28:18,301
But take the Princess somewhere safe.

255
00:28:18,479 --> 00:28:20,299
As you order, my Bey.

256
00:28:21,290 --> 00:28:25,290
After we attack Alişar's mansion,
not only with him, but we will also...

257
00:28:25,810 --> 00:28:28,160
... become enemies
with Geyhatu, my Bey.

258
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:30,420
As you know, Böke is with him.

259
00:28:32,676 --> 00:28:34,576
Its too late, Boran.

260
00:28:35,426 --> 00:28:39,426
Now I'll be enemies with
the entire world if necessary.

261
00:28:41,530 --> 00:28:44,710
Its time to be brave, brothers!

262
00:28:45,155 --> 00:28:47,705
Remember, I don't want any mistakes!

263
00:28:47,941 --> 00:28:49,621
Let's go!

264
00:29:07,710 --> 00:29:10,740
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)

265
00:29:10,801 --> 00:29:12,041
Let's go!

266
00:29:43,133 --> 00:29:45,373
Marinate these with honey.

267
00:29:45,715 --> 00:29:50,795
There will be a wedding and
a feast after iftar.

268
00:30:11,397 --> 00:30:13,607
What do you want from me?

269
00:30:16,527 --> 00:30:19,387
- Osman.
- I don't know where Osman is.

270
00:30:20,366 --> 00:30:24,516
Only thing I know is that he won't stop
before crushing the heads of...

271
00:30:24,516 --> 00:30:26,996
...a rat like you and
a snake like Sofia.

272
00:30:40,065 --> 00:30:42,815
You will pay for this, Alişar Bey.

273
00:30:45,778 --> 00:30:49,778
You will dream of those when you're
rotting in Geyhatu's hareem.

274
00:30:50,618 --> 00:30:54,398
I'd rather die than marry
that barbarian names Geyhatu.

275
00:30:54,398 --> 00:30:59,416
Neither he nor I care whether if
you're Geyhatu's woman or not.

276
00:31:00,264 --> 00:31:03,984
- Where is Osman?
- I wouldn't tell you even if I knew.

277
00:31:28,694 --> 00:31:32,694
I give you a single chance to be free.
How does Osman know you?

278
00:31:33,367 --> 00:31:35,937
Who from Byzantine is he working with?

279
00:31:35,937 --> 00:31:37,927
Tell me everything you know!

280
00:31:37,927 --> 00:31:42,957
Let's see if you can be
this brave once he is here, Alişar Bey!

281
00:32:09,397 --> 00:32:11,667
Hang her to the ceiling from her arms.

282
00:32:12,024 --> 00:32:15,664
Don't give her anything until she talks.

283
00:32:16,625 --> 00:32:19,065
Let's see how long she'll last.

284
00:32:38,280 --> 00:32:40,630
- It's more sturdy now, my Bey.
- Thank you.

285
00:32:40,630 --> 00:32:43,260
If you allow, we're ready to get going.

286
00:32:43,260 --> 00:32:47,050
We lost a lot of time.
Let's get going as soon as possible.

287
00:32:47,821 --> 00:32:51,421
Hatuns! Let's go!
Let's go.

288
00:33:02,217 --> 00:33:05,617
Ambush!
Ambush!

289
00:33:32,732 --> 00:33:33,922
Osman!

290
00:34:51,919 --> 00:34:52,969
Osman!

291
00:34:53,942 --> 00:34:59,522
What do you think you're doing?
Huh? What do you think you're doing?

292
00:35:00,009 --> 00:35:02,359
We know what we're doing, uncle.

293
00:35:03,710 --> 00:35:07,790
- Drop your weapon.
- What if I don't?

294
00:35:07,970 --> 00:35:10,950
What if I don't? Will you kill me?

295
00:35:11,845 --> 00:35:15,115
Not even the bandits ambush
a caravan going to a wedding.

296
00:35:15,115 --> 00:35:17,425
Aren't you ashamed of what you're doing?

297
00:35:18,601 --> 00:35:22,971
Is this how brave you are?
Be ashamed.

298
00:35:23,577 --> 00:35:27,267
Alps! Drop your weapons!

299
00:35:34,140 --> 00:35:36,760
Don't make us spill a brother's blood.

300
00:35:37,505 --> 00:35:38,385
Do it.

301
00:37:21,968 --> 00:37:23,398
Take my life.

302
00:37:24,412 --> 00:37:26,132
Take my life!

303
00:37:26,661 --> 00:37:34,811
Kill me! If you don't kill me,
I swear I'll kill you all one by one!

304
00:37:34,906 --> 00:37:36,456
Take my life!

305
00:37:36,994 --> 00:37:37,874
Take it!

306
00:37:38,258 --> 00:37:39,398
Take my life.

307
00:37:48,495 --> 00:37:52,725
Osman is going to ambush
my uncle Dündar...

308
00:37:52,725 --> 00:37:55,165
... while he's going
to Alişar's mansion, aunt.

309
00:38:01,740 --> 00:38:05,390
Osman wants to solve this
without spilling any blood.

310
00:38:06,830 --> 00:38:11,420
He wants to hinder Alişar's game
by showing Aygül the truth.

311
00:38:15,398 --> 00:38:19,398
Things will get out of control if any
blood is spilt, Allah forbid.

312
00:38:20,139 --> 00:38:23,089
The Tent will light up from
the inside and...

313
00:38:23,089 --> 00:38:26,519
... no one will be able
the put that fire out. You know that.

314
00:38:26,519 --> 00:38:28,739
There is no other way, aunt.

315
00:38:30,241 --> 00:38:34,551
Osman will use Dündar and Aygül
to lure Alişar into his trap.

316
00:38:35,017 --> 00:38:36,417
There is no other way.

317
00:38:36,417 --> 00:38:41,447
Dündar's Alps and Beys won't
be getting what they want.

318
00:38:42,671 --> 00:38:49,681
My Osman will both make his uncle open
his eyes and expel this trouble of ours.

319
00:38:52,682 --> 00:38:56,422
Now, we need to hold tight.

320
00:38:56,610 --> 00:39:00,610
What about, Bahadır? Him appearing so
suddenly seems suspicious to me.

321
00:39:01,262 --> 00:39:03,182
Bahadır is an orphan, aunt.

322
00:39:03,844 --> 00:39:07,844
My uncle ignores him
so he's finding a place to stay in.

323
00:39:08,792 --> 00:39:11,342
- No need to be suspicious.
- Son...

324
00:39:12,252 --> 00:39:15,152
You don't travel harsh roads
with a soft heart.

325
00:39:15,496 --> 00:39:17,946
Too much mercy will bring sickness.

326
00:39:18,309 --> 00:39:22,309
I know, I understand that you're related.
But...

327
00:39:23,242 --> 00:39:25,782
Don't be your feelings'
prisoner, my Gündüz.

328
00:39:27,267 --> 00:39:29,737
Bamsı Bey is right, my Gündüz.

329
00:39:31,722 --> 00:39:37,212
Dündar left the Tent.
But if you ask me...

330
00:39:38,419 --> 00:39:40,209
His ears are still here.

331
00:39:44,204 --> 00:39:50,914
What I mean is we need to be careful
about what we talk about next to Bahadır.

332
00:39:56,071 --> 00:39:58,251
Maybe you're right, Bamsı Bey.

333
00:39:58,875 --> 00:40:02,525
I will be alert without
breaking Bahadır's heart.

334
00:40:02,639 --> 00:40:04,289
Don't you worry.

335
00:40:05,478 --> 00:40:07,468
May Allah protect us.

336
00:40:08,110 --> 00:40:10,670
- Amen.
- Amen, Selcan Hatun.

337
00:40:10,670 --> 00:40:14,060
- I will go alongside Bala Hatun.
- Okay.

338
00:40:16,285 --> 00:40:18,795
Thank you, Selcan Hatun. Thank you.

339
00:40:31,555 --> 00:40:34,615
It seems that they gave Aygül to Osman.

340
00:40:34,615 --> 00:40:39,755
It's obvious that Osman Bey regretted it
so he raised hell.

341
00:40:40,010 --> 00:40:43,410
Osman! Oh Osman!

342
00:41:01,917 --> 00:41:05,917
I won't let Alişar marry Aygül, he said.

343
00:41:31,382 --> 00:41:34,312
Bala Hatun! Easy there.

344
00:41:34,486 --> 00:41:36,816
Your speed is racing with
your shamelessness.

345
00:41:36,816 --> 00:41:39,816
We kick you out of the door and
you get in through the chimney.

346
00:41:39,816 --> 00:41:45,326
Aren't you ashamed?
You brought us bad luck.

347
00:41:45,643 --> 00:41:48,493
How much blood
do you want to be spilt?

348
00:41:48,493 --> 00:41:50,973
- Isn't it enough?
- Aygül sister...

349
00:41:51,252 --> 00:41:55,252
If you have big dreams,
keep your heart strong.

350
00:41:56,421 --> 00:41:58,521
It shouldn't fall in every struggle.

351
00:42:01,417 --> 00:42:05,417
If you raise that hand to me again,
I'll pull your eyes out.

352
00:42:09,518 --> 00:42:10,858
Bala Hatun!

353
00:42:11,945 --> 00:42:13,155
Bala Hatun!

354
00:42:15,296 --> 00:42:17,836
Gündüz Bey said that
everyone must stay in the Tent.

355
00:42:20,528 --> 00:42:23,678
- Giddy up!
- Bala Hatun! Where are you going?

356
00:42:45,410 --> 00:42:49,300
What do you think you're doing?
Fear Allah!

357
00:42:49,402 --> 00:42:52,932
Let me go!
Let me go!

358
00:42:57,526 --> 00:43:02,976
You ambush your uncle with
Balgay's dog, huh?

359
00:43:13,776 --> 00:43:17,776
Take our lives so we're
free from your malice, Osman.

360
00:43:18,205 --> 00:43:22,205
You hurt a lot of people, uncle.
You won't be dying that easily.

361
00:43:23,545 --> 00:43:25,755
You will pay for them first.

362
00:43:32,742 --> 00:43:36,742
Come on. Get on the car.

363
00:43:38,227 --> 00:43:40,717
We'll have a long talk with you.

364
00:43:42,684 --> 00:43:49,074
Alişar is almost here.
What will you do to me if I resist?

365
00:43:49,074 --> 00:43:52,364
- What will you do?
- I won't even touch you.

366
00:43:52,924 --> 00:43:58,304
But Zöhre Hatun collaborated
with the enemy.

367
00:44:01,330 --> 00:44:03,710
And my brother deemed her worthy of exile.

368
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:07,580
And I...

369
00:44:09,591 --> 00:44:13,321
... will take her life right
in front of your eyes!

370
00:44:25,709 --> 00:44:27,029
I'm afraid...

371
00:44:28,557 --> 00:44:31,137
... you'll actually do that
to your uncle, Osman.

372
00:44:32,128 --> 00:44:33,448
You'll do that too.

373
00:45:39,144 --> 00:45:44,704
Konur. Take them to
the secret beech with Göktuğ.

374
00:45:50,528 --> 00:45:52,628
Go to the mansion from there.

375
00:45:55,464 --> 00:45:57,774
Dumrul and Ayaz stay alert.

376
00:46:42,169 --> 00:46:43,189
Bala!

377
00:46:45,356 --> 00:46:46,856
Bala, my girl!

378
00:46:57,006 --> 00:46:58,016
Bala!

379
00:46:58,775 --> 00:47:02,575
Bala... My dark-eyed girl,
what did you do?

380
00:47:03,013 --> 00:47:06,533
- Selcan Hatun!
- What?

381
00:47:07,329 --> 00:47:09,819
Bala Hatun left the Tent on a horse!

382
00:47:09,819 --> 00:47:13,819
Gündüz Bey's orders, no one
leaves, I said. She didn't listen.

383
00:47:14,084 --> 00:47:17,224
She left in such a way that it looked
like her horse would burst!

384
00:47:17,224 --> 00:47:21,474
What are you saying? Go after her!
Find Bala, come on!

385
00:47:23,294 --> 00:47:27,814
My girl... What will I say to Osman
if we can't find Bala?

386
00:48:09,949 --> 00:48:12,209
Only you'll understand
how I feel, my Alaca.

387
00:48:14,953 --> 00:48:20,193
We thought we wore love as
wings on our backs...

388
00:48:22,626 --> 00:48:25,156
But it was a rope on our necks instead.

389
00:48:30,185 --> 00:48:31,315
See?

390
00:48:33,049 --> 00:48:35,049
It left us short of breath.

391
00:48:35,875 --> 00:48:37,795
Osman ripped our hearts out.

392
00:48:38,033 --> 00:48:42,033
How can I live without
looking at these eyes?

393
00:48:44,495 --> 00:48:47,905
I trusted you with my heart and my future.

394
00:48:50,983 --> 00:48:53,283
I'm here if you protect them.

395
00:48:58,481 --> 00:49:02,481
If you give up, I won't be mad.
Remember that.

396
00:49:05,922 --> 00:49:07,122
Then...

397
00:49:09,284 --> 00:49:11,584
...this is the promise of Osman the Black.

398
00:49:13,383 --> 00:49:14,973
Remember well.

399
00:49:16,389 --> 00:49:22,299
Wherever you go, I'm right behind you.

400
00:49:24,727 --> 00:49:26,047
I swear!

401
00:49:30,544 --> 00:49:32,944
We went through such incidents.

402
00:49:34,207 --> 00:49:36,447
Such much has happened.

403
00:49:37,709 --> 00:49:39,929
Osman put everything to
the side and said...

404
00:49:39,929 --> 00:49:42,479
..."I won't let Alişar
marry Aygül", Alaca!

405
00:49:44,063 --> 00:49:46,303
How can my heart not burn?

406
00:50:31,417 --> 00:50:34,287
If he doesn't tolerate Aygül's marriage
that much...

407
00:50:36,991 --> 00:50:38,301
...what can we say?

408
00:50:41,183 --> 00:50:43,833
May Allah unite her with Osman bey.

409
00:50:51,533 --> 00:50:53,543
My reliever is my father.

410
00:51:00,666 --> 00:51:02,106
He will calm us down.

411
00:51:04,297 --> 00:51:06,257
He'll give peace to our souls certainly.

412
00:51:07,083 --> 00:51:08,113
Am I right?

413
00:51:30,178 --> 00:51:31,638
Come on, my girl.

414
00:51:31,850 --> 00:51:32,550
Come on!

415
00:51:39,346 --> 00:51:40,386
You will regret.

416
00:51:41,244 --> 00:51:42,694
But It will be too late.

417
00:51:44,120 --> 00:51:46,640
Dündar Bey rules thinking about everyone.

418
00:51:47,503 --> 00:51:50,593
Gündüz Bey rules at his will.

419
00:51:58,286 --> 00:52:02,906
When everyone hears about this,
then I'll see what you do.

420
00:52:04,151 --> 00:52:05,941
I don't know, Zöhre Hatun.

421
00:52:06,243 --> 00:52:08,243
I do what Osman bey orders.

422
00:52:09,962 --> 00:52:11,312
Where is my father?

423
00:52:11,525 --> 00:52:13,015
Where did you take him to?

424
00:52:13,736 --> 00:52:17,276
Are you afraid of two women whose
hands are tied?

425
00:52:21,789 --> 00:52:24,059
You don't have the right to know that.

426
00:52:24,169 --> 00:52:26,239
I am not allowed to say that as well.

427
00:52:29,235 --> 00:52:30,275
Now, be silent.

428
00:52:30,822 --> 00:52:31,972
I'll do my job.

429
00:52:32,475 --> 00:52:33,325
Come on.

430
00:52:49,409 --> 00:52:53,369
Do you take pleasure doing
this to your uncle, Osman?

431
00:52:55,152 --> 00:52:57,152
You did it, uncle.

432
00:52:59,797 --> 00:53:03,537
A lot of soldiers of us died just
because of you.

433
00:53:05,010 --> 00:53:08,750
Also, you killed my son.

434
00:53:10,977 --> 00:53:14,547
Moreover, you tried to kill me.

435
00:53:15,853 --> 00:53:20,953
If you feel comfortable about this,
kill me here.

436
00:53:21,632 --> 00:53:23,312
You're carrying my ancestor blood.

437
00:53:25,766 --> 00:53:27,866
I can't take responsibility by
killing you.

438
00:53:32,603 --> 00:53:37,723
I curse the day you were born!

439
00:53:43,737 --> 00:53:45,587
You're testing my patience.

440
00:53:50,244 --> 00:53:54,244
Do you think I don't know that
you are doing some dirty things?

441
00:53:57,276 --> 00:54:00,396
From where did you find the laws of
Cengizhan, Osman?

442
00:54:03,889 --> 00:54:06,519
That princess you brought to Tent...

443
00:54:07,550 --> 00:54:10,440
Who says something to you?

444
00:54:11,313 --> 00:54:13,483
Who is chasing you down an alley?

445
00:54:14,386 --> 00:54:17,176
Who is behind you, Osman?

446
00:54:17,642 --> 00:54:22,282
Whose pawn have you become that you
help them?

447
00:54:22,495 --> 00:54:23,195
Answer.

448
00:54:25,755 --> 00:54:27,915
I have my limits and you exceeded it.

449
00:54:29,711 --> 00:54:32,311
Now, answer me like a man.

450
00:54:50,411 --> 00:54:52,231
Don't ever tell a lie.

451
00:54:54,512 --> 00:54:55,852
I know everything.

452
00:54:57,415 --> 00:54:58,345
Everything!

453
00:55:06,673 --> 00:55:08,893
Do you know why I'm not killing you,
uncle?

454
00:55:13,941 --> 00:55:16,291
Because you are putty in the hands
of Alisar.

455
00:55:19,160 --> 00:55:21,280
I don't kill you because I feel
sorry for you.

456
00:55:23,584 --> 00:55:30,884
I know that you prevent Alisar so that
he couldn't kill Abdurrahman Gazi.

457
00:55:33,956 --> 00:55:39,976
I know that his dog, Melik, is trying
to kill Abdurrahman Gazi without mercy.

458
00:55:42,847 --> 00:55:47,447
How do you know these, Osman?

459
00:55:52,783 --> 00:55:56,783
Abdurrahman Gazi and Kılıç Alp are alive.

460
00:56:07,702 --> 00:56:09,352
I learned everything from them.

461
00:56:48,564 --> 00:56:50,744
Dündar Bey should have come till now.

462
00:56:51,289 --> 00:56:52,629
He is about to arrive.

463
00:56:52,878 --> 00:56:54,398
He'll come now, my bey.

464
00:56:54,886 --> 00:56:57,246
Adorn everywhere with spring flowers.

465
00:56:57,801 --> 00:57:00,481
I want to welcome Aygül Hatun with
pretty scents.

466
00:57:03,189 --> 00:57:07,699
Why are you behaving like that when we
have that much of trouble, Alişar Bey?

467
00:57:08,608 --> 00:57:12,348
Is it because you're going to marry?

468
00:57:14,386 --> 00:57:19,206
Our job is hard when there is huge Kayı
Tent behind Osman.

469
00:57:20,342 --> 00:57:22,922
Didn't you understand it still, commander
Böke?

470
00:57:23,645 --> 00:57:28,965
The ring I'll wear on Aygül's finger
will be a collar for her father.

471
00:57:30,753 --> 00:57:33,743
If you take Kayı Tent against you
in these lands...

472
00:57:34,271 --> 00:57:37,321
...you'll be surprised like Balgay
sooner or later.

473
00:57:38,815 --> 00:57:39,995
We'll see.

474
00:57:41,998 --> 00:57:45,698
From now on, the lady of my mansion is
Aygül Hatun.

475
00:57:46,010 --> 00:57:49,560
Tell the workers that they should do
whatever she wants.

476
00:57:50,499 --> 00:57:51,959
Order is order, my bey.

477
00:57:57,358 --> 00:57:58,588
What do you want?

478
00:57:58,688 --> 00:58:00,608
There has been a raid in Karaca, my bey.

479
00:58:00,698 --> 00:58:02,318
Bandits have taken a vehicle.

480
00:58:02,562 --> 00:58:04,092
There are blood trails.

481
00:58:04,158 --> 00:58:05,278
They're new.

482
00:58:05,367 --> 00:58:06,317
Vehicle?

483
00:58:06,925 --> 00:58:08,565
What's happening, Alişar Bey?

484
00:58:09,626 --> 00:58:11,706
Get the soldiers ready right now,
Melik.

485
00:58:11,740 --> 00:58:12,670
And my horse.

486
00:58:12,680 --> 00:58:13,400
Hurry!

487
00:58:16,171 --> 00:58:18,071
Where are you going, Alişar Bey?

488
00:58:19,164 --> 00:58:21,354
Dündar Bey should have come till now.

489
00:58:21,473 --> 00:58:23,853
There is something we don't know,
commander Böke.

490
00:58:24,241 --> 00:58:25,701
Do you think it is Osman?

491
00:58:26,111 --> 00:58:28,261
Osman is the cause of every disaster.

492
00:58:29,136 --> 00:58:30,416
Now, we'll understand.

493
00:58:30,660 --> 00:58:31,520
Let's go.

494
00:58:34,225 --> 00:58:35,175
Bring it quickly!

495
00:59:01,061 --> 00:59:03,191
The jackal got out of his mansion.

496
00:59:19,950 --> 00:59:23,990
Abdurrahman Gazi is alive, huh?

497
00:59:32,036 --> 00:59:33,516
Your every word is a lie.

498
00:59:34,358 --> 00:59:37,738
My word is right as much as
I didn't kill your son Baturay.

499
00:59:38,751 --> 00:59:43,191
Alişar kidnapped you from
Abdurrahman Gazi, not Balgay.

500
00:59:44,221 --> 00:59:48,851
In order to use you by hiding your faults
and provoking you, uncle.

501
00:59:48,973 --> 00:59:50,263
Open your eyes!

502
00:59:50,589 --> 00:59:52,119
Don't you see, uncle?

503
00:59:53,781 --> 00:59:58,361
There is lie and hypocrisy
in every word of you, Osman.

504
00:59:59,221 --> 01:00:03,851
The dog of Balgay, Kongar.
He was even with you.

505
01:00:04,428 --> 01:00:06,158
I saw it with my own eyes.

506
01:00:06,596 --> 01:00:08,226
Will you deny that as well?

507
01:00:08,851 --> 01:00:14,801
Don't you realize that I know you made alliance
with Balgay to ascend the throne of Kayı?

508
01:00:15,002 --> 01:00:20,302
If I wanted to do so, I would have killed
you already, uncle.

509
01:00:21,788 --> 01:00:24,018
Osman...

510
01:00:26,624 --> 01:00:29,364
Who knows what're you trying to do?

511
01:00:29,624 --> 01:00:32,604
Who knows what're you waiting for?

512
01:00:33,648 --> 01:00:36,588
Aren't you the one that sacrifice
his own daughter for greed?

513
01:00:37,114 --> 01:00:42,024
Your son, Batur, died because of your
greed.

514
01:00:42,198 --> 01:00:47,548
You don't even see that Alişar
who you'd trusted so much killed your son.

515
01:01:00,256 --> 01:01:01,286
That's enough.

516
01:01:01,317 --> 01:01:02,785
That's enough, Osman.

517
01:01:02,815 --> 01:01:04,523
I don't believe any word of you.

518
01:01:06,173 --> 01:01:10,173
In order to comfort yourself,
you ignore even the truth.

519
01:01:11,868 --> 01:01:14,558
You've always wanted my father throne.

520
01:01:15,136 --> 01:01:18,906
With his absence, you couldn't stop
being greedy.

521
01:01:19,520 --> 01:01:23,620
You're doing business with Alişar who
you're suspicious for killing your son.

522
01:01:24,221 --> 01:01:25,291
That's enough, Osman.

523
01:01:25,366 --> 01:01:26,566
That's enough!

524
01:01:26,637 --> 01:01:27,737
That's enough.

525
01:01:28,244 --> 01:01:29,514
I promise...

526
01:01:30,029 --> 01:01:32,679
I'll kill you with my own hands one day.

527
01:01:34,432 --> 01:01:41,872
Either kill me here today or
wait the day you will die.

528
01:01:45,319 --> 01:01:47,259
I'll confront you with Alişar, uncle.

529
01:01:48,112 --> 01:01:50,532
When you hear the truth from him...

530
01:01:51,098 --> 01:01:55,098
...your death will be because of your
grief, not because of me.

531
01:02:02,972 --> 01:02:03,722
Boran.

532
01:02:03,799 --> 01:02:04,749
Yes, my bey.

533
01:02:05,909 --> 01:02:07,429
Take my uncle from here.

534
01:02:10,323 --> 01:02:11,703
I don't want to see him.

535
01:02:31,353 --> 01:02:32,213
Osman.

536
01:02:34,910 --> 01:02:39,220
One day, there will be doomsday.

537
01:03:33,464 --> 01:03:34,274
Aunt?

538
01:03:34,294 --> 01:03:35,664
What happened, Selcan Hatun?

539
01:03:35,810 --> 01:03:37,160
Why're you worrying?

540
01:03:37,623 --> 01:03:39,113
Bala Hatun has gone.

541
01:03:39,133 --> 01:03:40,143
Where, aunt?

542
01:03:40,603 --> 01:03:44,403
He heard the words of Osman saying
that he won't allow Aygül to marry Alişar.

543
01:03:44,568 --> 01:03:45,788
She was confused.

544
01:03:45,894 --> 01:03:47,274
I couldn't think of it.

545
01:03:48,509 --> 01:03:52,279
Everybody knows the love of Osman.

546
01:03:52,419 --> 01:03:53,939
Why did she behave like this?

547
01:03:54,089 --> 01:03:56,049
Because of her love, Bamsi Bey.

548
01:03:56,455 --> 01:03:59,785
When she heard the words of
Osman saying he won't allow her...

549
01:03:59,881 --> 01:04:03,221
...she couldn't stay there anymore.

550
01:04:05,079 --> 01:04:06,489
I get her followed.

551
01:04:06,877 --> 01:04:08,907
But I don't think she will be found.

552
01:04:09,976 --> 01:04:11,586
What are we gonna do?

553
01:04:12,014 --> 01:04:13,244
Wait, wait, aunt.

554
01:04:13,834 --> 01:04:15,534
We'll find a solution surely.

555
01:04:16,208 --> 01:04:20,788
We should find, or else I have
nothing to say Osman, son.

556
01:05:28,923 --> 01:05:30,433
This is the mark of Kayı.

557
01:05:34,398 --> 01:05:36,208
The fight has occurred in here.

558
01:05:38,244 --> 01:05:39,944
There is blood trail on the floor.

559
01:06:36,347 --> 01:06:38,447
Janissary headgear of Dündar Bey.

560
01:06:38,934 --> 01:06:41,034
His headgear is here, but
he's not here.

561
01:06:42,325 --> 01:06:45,845
The clash has occurred in here but there
isn't any corpse.

562
01:06:47,423 --> 01:06:49,833
It's apparent that he wants you
to come somewhere.

563
01:06:51,497 --> 01:06:53,017
Let's follow the traces.

564
01:06:53,181 --> 01:06:57,181
Didn't you understand till now that
how wise guy Osman is, Melik?

565
01:06:57,809 --> 01:07:01,569
Do you think a troublesome guy like
Osman will leave evidence behind him?

566
01:07:02,275 --> 01:07:05,905
If you follow the traces, the only
thing you'll find is your grave.

567
01:07:07,272 --> 01:07:09,202
What're we going to do, my bey?

568
01:07:09,978 --> 01:07:11,678
There is only one thing to be done.

569
01:07:13,128 --> 01:07:15,238
I'll go to Kayı Tent and call
them to account.

570
01:07:15,315 --> 01:07:17,235
Then, let us come with you, my bey.

571
01:07:17,586 --> 01:07:18,806
You stay with Böke.

572
01:07:19,026 --> 01:07:24,676
Right. You know here well. There
is a lot of ways to pursue them.

573
01:07:24,875 --> 01:07:25,585
Soldiers.

574
01:07:26,155 --> 01:07:30,475
Gather whoever you find. You will
enter into commander Böke's service.

575
01:07:31,094 --> 01:07:31,914
Alişar Bey.

576
01:07:32,256 --> 01:07:33,786
I need Osman alive.

577
01:07:33,786 --> 01:07:34,996
Don't forget that.

578
01:07:35,759 --> 01:07:41,439
If we don't learn who is behind him,
after that we will be dead.

579
01:07:57,112 --> 01:07:59,132
Now you take the bait,
Alişar.

580
01:08:09,253 --> 01:08:10,343
Come on then!

581
01:08:11,251 --> 01:08:13,421
You fall into the trap of Osman.

582
01:08:14,259 --> 01:08:15,439
Come, Alişar.

583
01:08:16,237 --> 01:08:16,997
Come.

584
01:09:11,012 --> 01:09:13,222
Anyone didn't see you or hear you,
right?

585
01:09:13,363 --> 01:09:17,363
You invited us, we came here as if
we were walking in water, Bahadır Bey.

586
01:09:18,594 --> 01:09:22,434
No one saw and heard anything.

587
01:09:24,591 --> 01:09:29,001
When Osman killed your brother Baturay,
your father stumbled a lot, Bahadır Bey.

588
01:09:29,828 --> 01:09:33,278
Fortunately, you came back and
he reached the strength to endure.

589
01:09:33,358 --> 01:09:35,218
Your coming back made him alive again.

590
01:09:35,250 --> 01:09:36,750
But no one will know it.

591
01:09:37,790 --> 01:09:41,230
Osman and his friends should think
I am in bad with my father...

592
01:09:42,236 --> 01:09:43,846
...so that he has a deficit.

593
01:09:47,660 --> 01:09:49,800
We feel the fire of revenge
in your heart.

594
01:09:50,083 --> 01:09:51,683
We're proud of you, my bey.

595
01:09:52,083 --> 01:09:54,613
Order and then we take our revenge.

596
01:09:57,944 --> 01:10:00,214
Finally, that blessed time has come.

597
01:10:01,756 --> 01:10:05,606
In the night of the wedding, We will spill
out hatred against them...

598
01:10:05,978 --> 01:10:08,098
...and choke our enemies.

599
01:10:09,235 --> 01:10:11,295
Why are we waiting for the wedding,
my bey?

600
01:10:11,357 --> 01:10:13,457
The wedding will be in the mansion.

601
01:10:13,991 --> 01:10:20,001
The people of Kayı and Bey's of Tent, they
will go to Eskihisar as a guest of Alişar Bey.

602
01:10:24,263 --> 01:10:30,313
When they come back to the Tent,
their new Bey will greet them.

603
01:10:41,275 --> 01:10:42,975
Where is my father, mother?

604
01:10:43,450 --> 01:10:45,530
They didn't kill him, did they?

605
01:10:53,953 --> 01:10:55,703
They didn't, my daughter.

606
01:11:00,397 --> 01:11:02,547
Fortunately, my father.

607
01:11:02,836 --> 01:11:03,846
Fortunately.

608
01:11:08,169 --> 01:11:10,319
Fortunately, you're good, my bey.

609
01:11:23,700 --> 01:11:28,160
Do you really call this situation good,
my wife?

610
01:11:31,756 --> 01:11:33,536
May Allah help us.

611
01:11:35,351 --> 01:11:36,401
Amen.

612
01:12:03,715 --> 01:12:05,915
What're you doing, huh?

613
01:12:08,086 --> 01:12:10,156
Where are you taking my daughter to?

614
01:12:15,116 --> 01:12:16,536
Set free my daughter.

615
01:12:16,720 --> 01:12:17,900
Dündar Bey!

616
01:12:18,117 --> 01:12:19,071
What're you doing?

617
01:12:19,251 --> 01:12:20,155
Dündar Bey!

618
01:12:20,265 --> 01:12:20,915
Boran.

619
01:12:22,294 --> 01:12:23,194
Boran.

620
01:12:23,567 --> 01:12:25,027
What're you doing?

621
01:12:25,799 --> 01:12:27,029
Set free my daughter.

622
01:12:27,070 --> 01:12:28,070
Set free!

623
01:12:28,192 --> 01:12:30,182
Where are you taking my Aygül to?

624
01:12:30,416 --> 01:12:32,196
Didn't we sort it out?

625
01:12:32,823 --> 01:12:34,573
Osman Bey ordered so.

626
01:12:35,135 --> 01:12:35,945
Boran!

627
01:12:36,236 --> 01:12:36,966
Boran!

628
01:12:37,373 --> 01:12:39,663
Where are you taking my daughter to?

629
01:12:41,931 --> 01:12:42,781
Boran!

630
01:12:43,236 --> 01:12:47,126
If something happens to my Aygül,
I swear I'll kill all of you...

631
01:12:47,624 --> 01:12:51,584
...and establish Kayı Tent again
on your graves, Boran.

632
01:12:51,904 --> 01:12:52,774
Boran!

633
01:12:54,241 --> 01:12:55,311
Osman!

634
01:12:56,217 --> 01:12:58,837
What's your problem with Aygül?

635
01:13:00,791 --> 01:13:02,391
What are you planning?

636
01:13:02,536 --> 01:13:04,326
What's your problem, Osman.

637
01:13:04,760 --> 01:13:06,130
Osman!

638
01:13:36,247 --> 01:13:40,247
Did you start to be bandit by putting
away the soldiery and morals, Osman Bey?

639
01:14:05,211 --> 01:14:07,821
The bandit is walking around you, Aygül.

640
01:14:08,945 --> 01:14:10,675
But you don't want to see.

641
01:14:11,011 --> 01:14:13,121
I saw what I should see, Osman Bey.

642
01:14:13,197 --> 01:14:14,967
You've killed my brother.

643
01:14:15,167 --> 01:14:16,987
Now, you're being unfair to my family.

644
01:14:17,291 --> 01:14:22,801
If I had wanted to kill him, I would have
killed Batur in front of the Tent.

645
01:14:25,534 --> 01:14:26,504
But I didn't.

646
01:14:29,000 --> 01:14:32,600
As for your family, Alişar
cheats them.

647
01:14:32,707 --> 01:14:33,707
Alişar, huh?

648
01:14:34,486 --> 01:14:38,056
Do you know who embraced us when we're
expelled from the Tent, Osman Bey?

649
01:14:38,415 --> 01:14:40,605
Who saved my father and had him treated?

650
01:14:40,767 --> 01:14:42,867
Who saved us from your cruelty?

651
01:14:43,857 --> 01:14:46,347
Now you're talking about
the plans of Alişar.

652
01:14:46,448 --> 01:14:47,778
Why did he do these things?

653
01:14:48,525 --> 01:14:50,455
Is it just because he loves you so much?

654
01:14:50,613 --> 01:14:52,843
I don't know how much he loved me or us.

655
01:14:52,918 --> 01:14:55,598
But it's apparent that he loves us
more than you do.

656
01:15:00,696 --> 01:15:02,916
Now that you were so fond of us, then...

657
01:15:03,265 --> 01:15:06,365
...why didn't you marry me?

658
01:15:20,358 --> 01:15:21,708
Aygül...

659
01:15:22,477 --> 01:15:24,867
I loved you in a different way.

660
01:15:26,947 --> 01:15:29,437
I saw you as my sister.

661
01:15:31,227 --> 01:15:33,937
I wanted to protect you.

662
01:15:34,683 --> 01:15:36,683
But...

663
01:15:37,842 --> 01:15:40,562
you thought the other way.

664
01:15:43,090 --> 01:15:45,730
You didn't see me as I see you.

665
01:15:46,311 --> 01:15:49,221
What's my fault?

666
01:15:53,137 --> 01:15:58,977
Am I supposed to marry you to protect you
and think about your own good?

667
01:16:04,225 --> 01:16:05,645
Aygül...

668
01:16:06,838 --> 01:16:10,838
Don't see me as a stranger just for
that I didn't see you as another way.

669
01:16:11,164 --> 01:16:14,934
Don't hate me for not loving you back.

670
01:16:18,723 --> 01:16:22,723
Your hate will burn your future now.

671
01:16:25,722 --> 01:16:29,492
Alişar isn't a brave man as you think.

672
01:16:34,588 --> 01:16:36,968
He wants to exploit you.

673
01:16:37,136 --> 01:16:40,096
And I want to prevent it.

674
01:16:51,807 --> 01:16:52,967
I...

675
01:16:54,647 --> 01:16:57,907
...couldn't think about these, Osman Bey.

676
01:17:08,491 --> 01:17:11,511
I wish you're happy with Bala Hatun.

677
01:17:20,677 --> 01:17:24,807
Aygül, I love Bala Hatun.

678
01:17:27,648 --> 01:17:32,718
But I said that I won't let Aygül
be with Alişar.

679
01:17:35,845 --> 01:17:39,655
How can I help you more?

680
01:17:43,379 --> 01:17:48,779
I need your help to show
the truth to everyone.

681
01:17:50,414 --> 01:17:53,094
Help me like...

682
01:17:54,147 --> 01:17:56,837
I help you.

683
01:18:06,866 --> 01:18:09,436
What do you want from me, Osman Bey?

684
01:18:11,767 --> 01:18:17,297
My uncle is still my uncle, although
he's done so many bad things.

685
01:18:18,946 --> 01:18:21,846
I have to help him.

686
01:18:22,939 --> 01:18:26,489
I will make him confront with Alişar.

687
01:18:28,481 --> 01:18:31,081
I can't do it without your help.

688
01:18:33,450 --> 01:18:36,380
Are you brave enough to see the truth?

689
01:18:42,269 --> 01:18:43,759
I am.

690
01:18:56,205 --> 01:18:58,325
Then listen to me.

691
01:19:55,117 --> 01:19:57,557
Tell me, Gündüz.

692
01:19:57,777 --> 01:19:59,567
Where is Dündar Bey?

693
01:20:01,288 --> 01:20:04,798
He must have come to you.

694
01:20:05,960 --> 01:20:09,960
You tell me where my uncle is.

695
01:20:10,601 --> 01:20:13,561
I found Dündar Bey's cap in the woods.

696
01:20:13,598 --> 01:20:16,358
There were traces around it.

697
01:20:16,518 --> 01:20:19,048
What are you talking about, Alişar Bey?

698
01:20:21,544 --> 01:20:25,044
As you see, Alişar Bey.

699
01:20:25,060 --> 01:20:28,780
We don't know anything.

700
01:20:30,500 --> 01:20:34,650
If you don't know, then
why don't you look for him?

701
01:20:36,013 --> 01:20:40,143
I said I found his cap! Why
are you waiting!

702
01:21:04,703 --> 01:21:07,703
I'll tell the Alps.

703
01:21:08,246 --> 01:21:11,546
They will look for my uncle everywhere.

704
01:21:15,645 --> 01:21:18,395
Alişar, you should know that...

705
01:21:19,865 --> 01:21:23,185
if you have a finger in this situation
too...

706
01:21:25,409 --> 01:21:29,409
you won't have a head...

707
01:21:30,507 --> 01:21:31,797
...to wear a cap.

708
01:21:36,398 --> 01:21:40,598
You should know that, Gündüz...

709
01:21:42,280 --> 01:21:46,280
if your brother Osman has
a finger in it...

710
01:21:47,496 --> 01:21:50,906
...you won't have a tent to be a Bey for.

711
01:22:20,541 --> 01:22:22,161
Brother..

712
01:22:22,699 --> 01:22:26,699
...let me go with him.
I'll let you know.

713
01:22:55,179 --> 01:22:57,799
Look at us, Dündar Bey.

714
01:22:58,723 --> 01:23:02,113
We're a mess.

715
01:23:04,142 --> 01:23:06,322
His intention is clear, Hatun.

716
01:23:06,976 --> 01:23:09,136
He'll get rid of us first.

717
01:23:10,799 --> 01:23:14,329
We can't run away.

718
01:23:15,497 --> 01:23:18,067
Osman bides his time.

719
01:23:18,195 --> 01:23:22,295
It's us, then Gündüz and then...

720
01:23:23,245 --> 01:23:25,075
...whoever he sees.

721
01:23:26,282 --> 01:23:32,582
Osman will get rid of everyone
and rule the tent.

722
01:23:33,697 --> 01:23:37,147
I hope he drowns in his greed.

723
01:23:39,101 --> 01:23:40,921
I'm not afraid.

724
01:23:42,416 --> 01:23:45,216
You're still Dündar Bey.

725
01:23:46,407 --> 01:23:49,227
You have Alps and Beys.

726
01:23:49,804 --> 01:23:51,914
It's not that easy.

727
01:24:07,040 --> 01:24:12,590
You'll thank me because you're by my
side against ignoble Alişar.

728
01:24:12,762 --> 01:24:16,762
But I'm so grateful for him, even
if you call him ignoble.

729
01:24:18,198 --> 01:24:21,238
He protected me in such hard times.

730
01:24:22,102 --> 01:24:24,322
My good-hearted sister.

731
01:24:26,336 --> 01:24:30,336
You'll see who is Batur's killer and how
dangerous Alişar is for us...

732
01:24:30,910 --> 01:24:35,120
...when you do whatever I say.

733
01:24:37,366 --> 01:24:40,076
This marriage will be your mistake.

734
01:24:41,531 --> 01:24:44,261
Your biggest regret.

735
01:24:45,273 --> 01:24:47,313
Okay. What do you want?

736
01:24:47,892 --> 01:24:51,432
I'll do whatever you want.

737
01:24:52,791 --> 01:24:56,361
I hope we make it up as you said.

738
01:24:57,403 --> 01:24:58,533
Now...

739
01:24:59,033 --> 01:25:01,533
...you'll go to the palace and tell
him that...

740
01:25:02,275 --> 01:25:05,225
" My father hides in the woods."

741
01:25:05,264 --> 01:25:10,814
"He said we were abducted by Osman but
he learnt something big about Osman."

742
01:25:12,017 --> 01:25:15,627
"He wants to talk to you alone."

743
01:25:16,277 --> 01:25:20,277
"He said that you come alone."

744
01:25:21,096 --> 01:25:25,096
"He said that you two finish him finally."

745
01:25:27,087 --> 01:25:30,437
Bring Alişar to where I say and
I'll deal with the rest.

746
01:25:31,409 --> 01:25:35,069
Do it and let's finish this fight.

747
01:26:16,789 --> 01:26:19,829
- Salamun Alaikum, Osman.
- Alaikum Salam.

748
01:26:20,794 --> 01:26:24,504
You wear armour before your wound heals.

749
01:26:24,504 --> 01:26:27,364
You're in my war, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

750
01:26:28,718 --> 01:26:31,358
Give me your blessings.

751
01:26:32,084 --> 01:26:38,564
I fought with your grandfather Süleyman
Shah, your father Ertuğrul Ghazi.

752
01:26:38,596 --> 01:26:42,596
Thanks to my Allah...

753
01:26:42,596 --> 01:26:45,806
I fight with you too.

754
01:26:46,059 --> 01:26:50,659
- You give me your blessings.
- Thank you, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

755
01:26:51,165 --> 01:26:52,455
Thank you.

756
01:26:54,692 --> 01:26:57,092
Did we trap Alişar?

757
01:26:57,993 --> 01:27:00,113
As you said.

758
01:27:00,158 --> 01:27:05,108
When Dündar is late, Alişar and Böke
went out of the palace.

759
01:27:05,609 --> 01:27:08,759
They found Dündar's cap.

760
01:27:11,324 --> 01:27:15,014
- He must have gone crazy.
- Yes, my Bey.

761
01:27:15,082 --> 01:27:19,082
He went to the tent.

762
01:27:19,607 --> 01:27:24,547
He'll fall into our trap when
my brother says nothing.

763
01:27:26,516 --> 01:27:30,926
You should rest, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

764
01:27:31,348 --> 01:27:33,328
Kılıç Alp stays with me.

765
01:27:35,154 --> 01:27:37,624
I'll let you know if anything happens.

766
01:27:38,188 --> 01:27:40,658
Thank you, Osman.

767
01:27:44,579 --> 01:27:48,119
My Sheikh, we've been wandering in
this wood for days.

768
01:27:48,534 --> 01:27:51,684
Forgive me but...

769
01:27:52,661 --> 01:27:54,841
...what are we looking for?

770
01:28:01,883 --> 01:28:04,263
Our griefs, Zülfikar.

771
01:28:05,169 --> 01:28:07,149
Our griefs.

772
01:28:08,286 --> 01:28:11,866
The beginning of everything
starts with getting worried.

773
01:28:12,242 --> 01:28:17,362
When the Quran honours the earth...

774
01:28:18,748 --> 01:28:23,958
...those who believe just began
to understand oracles.

775
01:28:25,156 --> 01:28:30,406
But there was someone who was
uncomfortable with his life.

776
01:28:31,010 --> 01:28:35,340
He was worried about mankind and...

777
01:28:37,103 --> 01:28:39,573
...he felt that in his heart.

778
01:28:41,336 --> 01:28:46,126
That's why he settled in Mount Hira.

779
01:28:47,580 --> 01:28:51,900
He was our Prophet.

780
01:28:55,372 --> 01:28:57,602
He kept asking himself that...

781
01:28:58,588 --> 01:29:02,588
"What should I do? What should I do?"

782
01:29:03,626 --> 01:29:08,186
The first verses were about this grief.

783
01:29:09,077 --> 01:29:13,837
These were the remedies of that grief.

784
01:29:17,115 --> 01:29:19,675
Beard is a tradition
(in Islam), right Akça?

785
01:29:20,839 --> 01:29:22,869
Yes, my Sheikh.

786
01:29:26,931 --> 01:29:30,651
To greet is a tradition, right Zülfikar?

787
01:29:30,731 --> 01:29:32,271
Yes, my Sheikh.

788
01:29:33,803 --> 01:29:37,803
Eating with the right hand
is a tradition, right?

789
01:29:37,836 --> 01:29:40,106
Yes, my Sheikh.

790
01:29:40,486 --> 01:29:43,816
The most powerful tradition is...

791
01:29:43,896 --> 01:29:49,306
...to let people have the oracles.

792
01:29:50,551 --> 01:29:53,131
To grief with this.

793
01:29:55,540 --> 01:29:59,030
Our Allah gives our Prophet's duty...

794
01:30:00,006 --> 01:30:03,616
with the grief he has...

795
01:30:04,466 --> 01:30:06,396
...like this in Al-Muddaththir surah....

796
01:30:07,208 --> 01:30:11,208
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

797
01:30:12,469 --> 01:30:15,589
"You who covers himself
[with a garment],"

798
01:30:17,195 --> 01:30:19,665
"Arise and warn."

799
01:30:20,524 --> 01:30:24,134
"And your Lord glorify."

800
01:30:24,340 --> 01:30:29,390
"And your clothing purify, and
uncleanliness avoid."

801
01:30:31,577 --> 01:30:34,637
What is our duty, my Sheikh?

802
01:30:35,481 --> 01:30:38,331
Our Prophet...

803
01:30:38,331 --> 01:30:41,081
did his duty all his life.

804
01:30:42,639 --> 01:30:44,489
He tried hard...

805
01:30:44,594 --> 01:30:48,204
He made a civilization out of the
arid desert.

806
01:30:48,961 --> 01:30:52,961
Our duty is to follow this holy way.

807
01:30:54,527 --> 01:31:00,097
Our duty is to lighten this era's
darkness with oracle's lamps.

808
01:31:02,651 --> 01:31:05,351
But first...

809
01:31:06,055 --> 01:31:08,365
we should enlighten ourselves.

810
01:31:08,987 --> 01:31:12,627
It's because those who can't
enlighten themselves...

811
01:31:13,650 --> 01:31:18,400
can't enlighten the darkness.

812
01:31:19,818 --> 01:31:20,798
For instance...

813
01:31:22,027 --> 01:31:24,407
those who can't be awake...

814
01:31:24,875 --> 01:31:28,425
those who can't wake up...

815
01:31:28,907 --> 01:31:30,827
can't stand this grief.

816
01:31:32,310 --> 01:31:35,800
Those who don't believe...

817
01:31:36,341 --> 01:31:39,061
can't set up a civilization in this world.

818
01:31:40,633 --> 01:31:42,623
Don't forget, friends...

819
01:31:43,992 --> 01:31:48,662
If someone doesn't pray at night, he
can't be a fighter at day.

820
01:31:50,365 --> 01:31:56,665
Now it's time to try hard.

821
01:31:58,224 --> 01:32:02,374
Inshaallah, we'll set up our dervish
convent...

822
01:32:03,417 --> 01:32:06,397
- here.
- Inshaallah.

823
01:32:07,663 --> 01:32:11,663
This dervish convent...

824
01:32:13,043 --> 01:32:17,333
will be a precursor of a new founding.

825
01:32:45,870 --> 01:32:49,660
You're here without any news,
Commander Kongar. Alişar Bey isn't here.

826
01:32:50,255 --> 01:32:53,115
I know.

827
01:33:05,264 --> 01:33:06,834
Why did you come then?

828
01:33:08,871 --> 01:33:12,871
You tell me.

829
01:33:15,346 --> 01:33:16,816
Now tell me...

830
01:33:17,311 --> 01:33:19,301
Where is Alişar?

831
01:33:19,651 --> 01:33:22,771
Alişar Bey went to wherever he wanted.

832
01:33:23,717 --> 01:33:26,127
He accounts for neither me nor you.

833
01:33:30,276 --> 01:33:32,126
I call out...

834
01:33:33,325 --> 01:33:37,325
don't you know? I'll tell you!

835
01:33:56,382 --> 01:33:58,412
My brother.

836
01:33:59,564 --> 01:34:01,734
We have a revenge to take.

837
01:34:02,393 --> 01:34:04,203
We've just started.

838
01:34:48,190 --> 01:34:51,590
What's that? What's happening?

839
01:35:00,277 --> 01:35:03,397
Boran, what are you doing?

840
01:35:03,467 --> 01:35:05,527
Keep calm, Dündar Bey.

841
01:35:05,610 --> 01:35:08,410
Osman Bey wanted me to do it.

842
01:35:21,020 --> 01:35:23,100
Where are you taking them?

843
01:35:26,087 --> 01:35:28,177
Why don't you take me?

844
01:35:31,847 --> 01:35:33,947
What will you do?

845
01:35:34,416 --> 01:35:35,906
Take me.

846
01:35:36,103 --> 01:35:37,643
Take me!

847
01:35:39,154 --> 01:35:41,454
Where are we going, Boran?

848
01:35:42,866 --> 01:35:44,866
What will you do to us?

849
01:35:44,913 --> 01:35:46,153
Tell me.

850
01:35:46,304 --> 01:35:51,004
I do what Osman Bey wants, Dündar Bey.
Forgive me.

851
01:36:05,188 --> 01:36:08,208
Hatun, don't worry.

852
01:36:08,824 --> 01:36:12,824
I'll take care of Aygül, don't worry.

853
01:36:21,078 --> 01:36:22,178
Osman!

854
01:36:29,698 --> 01:36:32,428
Osman, don't!

855
01:36:32,550 --> 01:36:37,270
Don't hurt them! Don't!

856
01:36:38,544 --> 01:36:41,844
Take me. Take me, Osman!

857
01:36:51,066 --> 01:36:52,176
Osman.

858
01:36:53,916 --> 01:36:58,226
- What are you going to do?
- You'll see, uncle.

859
01:36:59,684 --> 01:37:03,684
You'll see when your eyes open
without greed.

860
01:37:20,849 --> 01:37:25,229
Don't hurt them!
Don't!

861
01:37:29,331 --> 01:37:34,241
Kill me. Don't hurt them! Don't hurt my
child and my Bey!

862
01:37:37,168 --> 01:37:41,168
Take me, Osman! Don't!

863
01:37:44,950 --> 01:37:47,180
Kill me instead of them!

864
01:37:48,638 --> 01:37:50,328
Don't!

865
01:38:15,966 --> 01:38:17,376
Princess.

866
01:38:20,352 --> 01:38:23,582
Alişar did this to you?

867
01:38:24,607 --> 01:38:26,217
It's okay.

868
01:38:27,651 --> 01:38:29,511
I'm fine, thanks to you.

869
01:38:35,845 --> 01:38:38,365
Çetinalp, protect Princess.

870
01:38:38,504 --> 01:38:40,474
Take her to where Osman Bey said.

871
01:38:40,536 --> 01:38:44,096
Protect her well.

872
01:38:44,456 --> 01:38:47,316
- Do you understand?
- Don't worry, Konuralp.

873
01:38:48,361 --> 01:38:51,131
Horses are outside. Let's go, princess.

874
01:38:53,060 --> 01:38:55,240
I'm grateful for everything.

875
01:38:56,418 --> 01:38:58,518
God bless you.

876
01:39:20,551 --> 01:39:23,851
I couldn't see their content.
I took all the papers.

877
01:39:23,881 --> 01:39:28,371
- Good, brother.
- Let's go before Alişar comes with his dogs.

878
01:39:28,445 --> 01:39:30,995
Get ready.

879
01:39:32,413 --> 01:39:35,313
Let's go silently
before Alişar and his dogs come.

880
01:39:37,113 --> 01:39:39,003
We took what we had to.

881
01:40:23,918 --> 01:40:26,018
Aygül.

882
01:40:26,382 --> 01:40:28,102
Come with me.

883
01:40:56,703 --> 01:40:58,443
Osman!

884
01:41:01,825 --> 01:41:04,055
Osman, what are you doing?

885
01:41:26,070 --> 01:41:28,040
You know what to do.

886
01:41:35,559 --> 01:41:37,329
I know, Osman Bey.

887
01:41:40,241 --> 01:41:41,431
Aygül!

888
01:41:43,560 --> 01:41:49,010
- Where are you going, my daughter?
- It's time you faced Alişar Bey, father.

889
01:41:55,752 --> 01:41:58,652
- Aygül...
- Sorry, father.

890
01:41:59,002 --> 01:42:01,822
Now, it's time to reveal the truth.

891
01:42:03,425 --> 01:42:07,629
What truth, Aygül?
What the hell are you talking about?

892
01:42:07,629 --> 01:42:10,459
Osman Bey will take you to Alişar Bey.

893
01:42:14,087 --> 01:42:16,369
Forgive me for doing this.

894
01:42:17,379 --> 01:42:22,309
I can't be a wife of someone who I doubt
that may have killed my brother.

895
01:42:28,396 --> 01:42:33,456
Aygül, stop!
Daughter, I'm talking to you!

896
01:42:33,576 --> 01:42:36,486
What do you think you are doing?

897
01:42:39,201 --> 01:42:42,821
Stop!
Daughter!

898
01:42:43,439 --> 01:42:47,789
Forgive me, father.
But I am doing the right thing.

899
01:42:52,951 --> 01:42:56,777
Aygül, come back here!

900
01:42:56,777 --> 01:43:01,137
I won't give you my blessings,
my daughter, come back here!

901
01:43:04,171 --> 01:43:07,631
- Aygül!
- Pull yourself together, uncle.

902
01:43:07,631 --> 01:43:10,801
Aygül doesn't want to marry
her brother's murderer.

903
01:43:11,562 --> 01:43:14,482
She's brave enough to reveal that.

904
01:43:15,488 --> 01:43:19,288
Now, it's your turn to be brave.

905
01:43:20,205 --> 01:43:22,455
You are going to face Alişar.

906
01:43:22,523 --> 01:43:27,167
You are using my daughter to
entrap Alişar.

907
01:43:27,167 --> 01:43:29,052
You are going to pay off, Osman!

908
01:43:29,052 --> 01:43:34,925
I will kill everyone who is with you!

909
01:43:34,925 --> 01:43:39,326
I will be your death!
I will ruin you!

910
01:43:39,326 --> 01:43:43,236
I will call you to account for what you
have done!

911
01:43:53,057 --> 01:43:54,397
Let's go.

912
01:44:14,439 --> 01:44:15,709
Let's go.

913
01:45:35,762 --> 01:45:37,392
There is no sign.

914
01:45:40,145 --> 01:45:43,235
We have been searching in the right area.

915
01:45:43,249 --> 01:45:48,282
I have gone hunting with Osman a lot.
It's hard to find him in the forest.

916
01:45:48,282 --> 01:45:51,302
I am not leaving until I find my sister
and father, Alişar Bey.

917
01:45:51,302 --> 01:45:54,772
You can leave if you have important things
to do.

918
01:45:56,449 --> 01:46:00,111
Aygül is your sister,
and she is my fiance.

919
01:46:00,631 --> 01:46:03,711
Dündar is your father,
and he is my friend.

920
01:46:04,513 --> 01:46:10,923
We are not leaving before we find them.

921
01:46:11,990 --> 01:46:15,997
- There's no use in searching.
- What do you mean, Commander Böke?

922
01:46:16,257 --> 01:46:19,687
Are you saying that we should leave
my sister and father to their fate?

923
01:46:19,989 --> 01:46:24,592
Osman will leave us a trace at the time
when he wants us to find him.

924
01:46:25,082 --> 01:46:29,462
He will draw us where he wants us to be.
We need to take cover.

925
01:46:29,472 --> 01:46:32,092
What's in your mind, Commander Böke?

926
01:46:39,196 --> 01:46:41,175
My Bey, can I?

927
01:46:41,545 --> 01:46:46,512
I will take it all out on you if you
don't say something important.

928
01:46:46,902 --> 01:46:51,952
My Bey, Osman Bey's Alps raided into
your mansion and abducted your guest.

929
01:46:57,346 --> 01:47:01,345
What are you saying!
Talk!

930
01:47:01,845 --> 01:47:04,513
Osman is strating to leave traces.

931
01:47:05,233 --> 01:47:07,425
Let's see who entraps first.

932
01:47:08,085 --> 01:47:10,325
Speak, I tell you!
Speak!

933
01:47:10,604 --> 01:47:15,904
The gate of the mansion was open when I
got there, there were bodies in the yard.

934
01:47:19,494 --> 01:47:20,814
Osman!

935
01:47:33,263 --> 01:47:35,917
This is now a feud.

936
01:47:36,437 --> 01:47:42,527
My Lord, execute either me or Osman!

937
01:47:45,017 --> 01:47:47,587
What are you waiting for, Melik?
Bring the horses!

938
01:47:48,299 --> 01:47:51,279
We are going to drink blood!

939
01:47:59,988 --> 01:48:02,988
I wish to be with you in the revenge day,
Alişar Bey.

940
01:48:03,003 --> 01:48:08,043
But, leave a couple of scouts of yours with
me, we'll inform you if we found anything.

941
01:48:10,886 --> 01:48:15,190
Inform every living in this land!

942
01:48:15,510 --> 01:48:20,331
From now on, everyone who is good with
him...

943
01:48:20,331 --> 01:48:24,946
... or respects him is my enemy!

944
01:48:25,226 --> 01:48:29,966
If someone is brave enough to face me,
let them come.

945
01:48:45,891 --> 01:48:47,990
What do you say, Commander Böke?

946
01:48:48,230 --> 01:48:53,093
It's like I said, if we
follow his traces...

947
01:48:53,093 --> 01:48:55,703
We will end up dead.

948
01:48:56,203 --> 01:49:03,453
But we are going to follow Osman,
not his traces.

949
01:49:44,601 --> 01:49:48,298
Our tribe has been in trouble since
you came here.

950
01:49:48,568 --> 01:49:54,328
Leave Osman alone, you cause trouble
to him.

951
01:50:37,915 --> 01:50:39,345
Alişar Bey.

952
01:50:45,285 --> 01:50:47,015
How did this happen?

953
01:50:47,850 --> 01:50:53,720
How can they get in my mansion freely?

954
01:50:54,608 --> 01:50:57,093
How could you let that happen?

955
01:50:57,093 --> 01:51:01,103
My Bey, It was Kongar.
He came with Nökers(soldiers).

956
01:51:01,103 --> 01:51:04,060
We didn't know he came to abduct
Princess.

957
01:51:04,060 --> 01:51:07,854
- Kongar?
- A wounded man of ours told us.

958
01:51:07,854 --> 01:51:10,164
Nökers(soldiers) were Osman's Alps.

959
01:51:10,164 --> 01:51:14,164
They saw Konur and Boran
disguised as Nökers, my Bey!

960
01:51:42,261 --> 01:51:43,731
Alişar Bey!

961
01:51:46,986 --> 01:51:49,106
I have things that I need to tell you.

962
01:51:49,169 --> 01:51:51,899
"My father is hiding in
a secret place in the forest."

963
01:51:51,899 --> 01:51:53,976
" Osman kidnapped us," he says.

964
01:51:53,976 --> 01:51:57,066
"But he learned something
important about Osman."

965
01:51:57,173 --> 01:52:00,453
"He wants to talk to you where
no one is present."

966
01:52:01,456 --> 01:52:05,456
"I want him to come alone, he said."

967
01:52:06,289 --> 01:52:10,289
"We will finally end Osman together!"
Tell him these.

968
01:52:11,911 --> 01:52:14,791
Osman kidnapped my father and mother.

969
01:52:15,345 --> 01:52:19,105
I know where he is. Only you can save us.

970
01:52:33,250 --> 01:52:36,890
Bismillâhirrahmânirrahîm.
(in the name of God, the merciful and compassionate.)

971
01:52:49,629 --> 01:52:51,799
Bismillâh.

972
01:53:00,810 --> 01:53:05,910
The time of iftar is near.
Let me continue from here, my Sheikh.

973
01:53:11,467 --> 01:53:15,697
Is working your duty and
not mine, my Akça?

974
01:53:15,697 --> 01:53:17,487
Not at all, my Sheikh.

975
01:53:24,918 --> 01:53:26,848
Bismillâh.

976
01:53:40,251 --> 01:53:41,901
My Sheikh!

977
01:53:47,461 --> 01:53:50,081
I've come to your side,
if you accept it.

978
01:53:56,271 --> 01:53:58,461
You've come at a good time, my daughter.

979
01:53:59,639 --> 01:54:04,119
You came after good news.

980
01:54:05,966 --> 01:54:09,056
You've come like the spring after winter.

981
01:54:09,527 --> 01:54:10,687
Welcome.

982
01:54:11,879 --> 01:54:13,459
You brought happiness.

983
01:54:20,306 --> 01:54:23,346
Did the good news fell on
the soil, my Sheikh?

984
01:54:26,663 --> 01:54:28,863
They fell on our hearts, my daughter.

985
01:54:31,912 --> 01:54:36,492
If Allah permits,
we'll build our lodge here.

986
01:54:40,075 --> 01:54:44,885
This lodge will be a warning base,
if Allah permits.

987
01:54:46,523 --> 01:54:51,733
The enemy is wild, trouble is diverse.

988
01:54:55,557 --> 01:55:01,067
But the worst danger awaiting
humans is the fire of hell.

989
01:55:02,045 --> 01:55:09,305
We'll warn.
Because warning is a lovers duty.

990
01:55:10,532 --> 01:55:12,382
How will we warn, my Sheikh?

991
01:55:13,368 --> 01:55:21,098
Like a mother warns her naughty child
of the dangers waiting for him...

992
01:55:22,158 --> 01:55:30,088
Like a master warns his apprentice
of the dangers waiting for them...

993
01:55:32,992 --> 01:55:37,582
Like a doctor treats her patience...

994
01:55:38,013 --> 01:55:43,333
We'll warn the people of Mohammad
the same way in this lodge.

995
01:55:44,531 --> 01:55:49,991
Hopefully, this lodge will be the place
of hope for a new establishment.

996
01:55:51,605 --> 01:55:55,315
In this lodge, we'll enlighten
those who are in the dark.

997
01:55:56,402 --> 01:55:59,522
We'll turn Alps into saints.

998
01:56:02,722 --> 01:56:07,612
From a filthy state, we'll fly
towards a great future.

999
01:56:09,353 --> 01:56:14,003
May our run be blessed, and
our lodge Mubarak!

1000
01:56:14,003 --> 01:56:16,823
- Amen.
- Amen.

1001
01:56:58,736 --> 01:57:05,956
Boran. We'll cut this malady like
the tumour on my grandfather's back!

1002
01:57:06,972 --> 01:57:10,002
- Hopefully, my Bey.
- Hopefully.

1003
01:57:10,002 --> 01:57:12,442
- Keep your eyes wide open.
- I will.

1004
01:57:15,827 --> 01:57:17,517
My Bey, ambush!

1005
01:59:09,144 --> 01:59:11,774
Mountains don't touch other mountains...

1006
01:59:12,625 --> 01:59:17,375
But people can reach other
people, Osman.

1007
01:59:29,406 --> 01:59:30,446
Aygül!

1008
01:59:56,174 --> 02:00:00,594
Aygül! My heart is on Bala Hatun.

1009
02:00:01,885 --> 02:00:11,185
I've come this mansion to make Alişar
Bey happy and spend my life by his side.

1010
02:00:12,757 --> 02:00:19,287
But don't forget that I came with
my pain, and not with a wedding.

1011
02:00:22,777 --> 02:00:25,697
My wedding will be today.

1012
02:00:26,166 --> 02:00:30,166
But the ceremony will be
the day Osman dies...

1013
02:00:30,166 --> 02:00:34,546
... who killed my brother and
kidnapped my father and mother.

1014
02:00:36,883 --> 02:00:42,053
This mansion will mourn until
the fire inside me is cooled down...

1015
02:00:42,053 --> 02:00:44,163
... with Osman's blood!

1016
02:00:45,143 --> 02:00:49,803
Now take out everything I see
that enhances my pain!

1017
02:00:50,925 --> 02:00:57,915
I'll be mourning on my man's mansion.
Remember that!

1018
02:01:26,903 --> 02:01:33,483
Aygül is waiting peacefully in her home
for his father to return.

1019
02:01:36,881 --> 02:01:38,221
And you...

1020
02:01:41,165 --> 02:01:45,305
Looks like the end of the road for you.

1021
02:02:19,231 --> 02:02:20,361
Father!

1022
02:02:22,376 --> 02:02:23,466
Bahadır!

1023
02:02:25,695 --> 02:02:27,345
Where is my father?

1024
02:02:30,464 --> 02:02:32,144
Where is my father?

1025
02:02:35,704 --> 02:02:39,704
You'll feel your father's wrath like
your brother Batur.

1026
02:02:41,441 --> 02:02:42,321
Don't.

1027
02:02:48,290 --> 02:02:51,120
Bahadır is like a son to me now.

1028
02:02:52,486 --> 02:02:59,206
I won't let you take his life like
you've taken Batur's life.

1029
02:03:11,196 --> 02:03:12,396
Bahadır!

1030
02:03:14,626 --> 02:03:18,846
Children suffer from their father's sins.

1031
02:03:25,554 --> 02:03:28,754
Don't. Don't you do it.

1032
02:03:29,508 --> 02:03:31,778
Don't you trust that dog Alişar.

1033
02:03:34,802 --> 02:03:38,052
You'll dig your father and
sister's grave yourself.

1034
02:03:39,146 --> 02:03:40,206
Don't.

1035
02:03:46,232 --> 02:03:54,162
They will rip your lungs to pieces when
I throw you to the hands of Geyhatu.

1036
02:03:55,254 --> 02:03:59,984
You won't even have a grave.
Osman...

1037
02:04:09,772 --> 02:04:12,712
Those who devote their
lives to their people...

1038
02:04:13,853 --> 02:04:16,803
... live longer than their executioners!

1039
02:04:16,803 --> 02:05:20,203
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com